    fix(cli): DF-H3-SHIM-FOREMAN-4 — pre-update-check names the matrix and lists supported versions
    
    The "no compatibility data for Hermes X" BLOCK was a dead end: it never named
    the versions.yaml that was consulted, never listed the Hermes versions that
    matrix supports, and said nothing at all when the matrix itself was empty.
    
    upgrade_check now resolves the effective matrix path once (an explicit
    versions_yaml_path when the caller passed one, else the module-level
    VERSIONS_YAML_PATH — bundled package data, dev-tree fallback) and builds the
    BLOCK message from that resolution: the consulted path is echoed as-is, the
    supported Hermes versions are listed ascending (ordered with the existing
    _parse_version helper, original strings preserved), and the target is annotated
    as newer than the newest / older than the oldest supported version when it falls
    outside the supported range. An empty, missing or unreadable matrix gets its own
    distinct message naming the path and the --versions-yaml / versions_yaml_path=
    escape hatch instead of printing an empty version list, and _load_version_matrix
    now reads a non-mapping YAML document or a non-list hermes_versions as an empty
    matrix instead of raising AttributeError.
    
    severity stays BLOCK for both cases and cli.py is untouched (it echoes
    result.message verbatim and still exits 1); the legacy lowercase phrase
    "no compatibility data" is preserved for scripts/smoke_test.sh.
    
    Addresses DF-H3-SHIM-FOREMAN-4.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
